WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:07.089
Indexes are physical structures that help PostgreSQL
find rows more efficiently Primary

00:00:07.115 --> 00:00:13.752
keys and UNIQUE constraints automatically receive
supporting unique indexes Foreign-key

00:00:13.766 --> 00:00:19.360
columns on the child side are different PostgreSQL
does not automatically create

00:00:19.374 --> 00:00:24.755
every child-side index for you Whether an index is
useful depends on

00:00:24.781 --> 00:00:31.110
actual query patterns joins updates deletes and data
volume Run

00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:36.678
the provided example and inspect the indexes At this
stage

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:41.404
you do not need to design a full indexing strategy
The important

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:46.114
idea is that logical relationships and physical
performance structures are related but

00:00:46.128 --> 00:00:52.477
not identical First design correct keys and
constraints Then

00:00:52.503 --> 00:00:56.411
add indexes based on real access patterns and
measured performance needs
